From fe5697ab1b916152ccebc550f236b46dcec54576 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 18:34:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] process completion custody survives a gateway
 restart between exit and watcher tick

A gateway-watched notify_on_complete job's exit was recorded in its result receipt, removed from
_running and from the checkpoint before the 5 s watcher tick. A gateway restart in that gap left
nothing to re-adopt (a receipt reads as observed), so the completion was never admitted
(proc_0fcf936312c4; exact kill interleaving unproven).

The receipt write now carries a delivery_obligation block (same atomic write, before checkpoint
removal) for gateway-routed notify_on_complete jobs not already consumed. It is settled only by
the watcher's admission (or found-admitted / intended suppression) or by wait/read_log/kill
consumption. recover_from_checkpoint(owner="gateway") re-arms a watcher for each owed receipt of
its own profile whose writer is gone, bounded by 48 h / 8 starts; the producer identity
(completion, proc id, started_at) makes a lost-ack replay resolve to the existing admission.
Ordinary receipts stay retrieval-only. CLI, managed workers and the TUI backend never adopt.

`python -m tools.process_registry_obligations show|reopen proc_<id>` inspects or re-owes one
exact receipt; reopen refuses when a completion admission for that identity exists.

Task: t_01a1d0f2824382ab
